44 he scored in 57 full internationals  jimmy grieves was an instinctive goal  scorer and truly one of the greats of  the game  to this day nobody has scored more top  flight goals in english football he  scored 44 goals for his country in 57  games in an international career that  spanned from 1959 to 1967.  the former striker played for chelsea  west ham and ac milan during his career  but it was for his time at tottenham  hotspur that he will be best remembered  greaves helped the england squad win the  1966 world cup despite famously not  being chosen to play in the final  but his contribution was honored in 2009  when he collected a medal from then  prime minister gordon brown for his role  in the world cup victory against germany  saint gravese ran from 1985 to 1992.  in 2015 jimmy suffered a severe stroke  which left him relying on a wheelchair  he'll be remembered by football fans  everywhere but it is perhaps for an  extraordinary spell at tottenham hotspur  which saw him become and still remain  the club's all-time top scorer with 266  goals  that he'll best be remembered  ender brady sky news
 

